  "summary": "Both records are substantially well-grounded, with strong restraint on human-subjects, consent, and preprocessing slots where the bundle supplies no evidence, and appropriate surfacing of source disagreements (Sali affiliation, project end date, release-date discrepancy, protein-count change). Three issues rise above cosmetic. First, the core record's distributions[].byte_size values are fabricated integer precision derived by decimal conversion from rounded Dataverse display strings; the full record correctly declined to populate total_size_bytes on the same evidence, making this an internal inconsistency as well as an unsupported claim. Second, created_on (both records) uses a 2025-02-27 Data Creation Date that the bundle shows is identical across all four releases and is therefore not specific to this one. Third, both descriptions assert that MDA-MB-468 perturb-seq data are included, which the release prose says but the ten-file inventory and the Embargoed external link do not bear out. Secondary issues: related_datasets and was_derived_from are omitted despite the bundle explicitly supporting typed lineage to four prior DOI-identified releases; total_file_count is populated in full but omitted in core on identical evidence; and the protein-count change is classified as errata when the bundle characterises it as neither an error nor a correction. Constructed identifiers for file_collections and subsets are necessary under the schema but are nowhere marked as minted rather than sourced."
